  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 556ecd75ee852ce4a93c60357c4eb4f6, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Dear friend,


    Giulia here, from the coast this time. I am on
    holiday near Naples, and I ate a salad so simple it made me cry a little.


    Caprese
    is only three things: buffalo mozzarella, ripe tomato, fresh basil. The colours
    of our flag. If even one of them is poor, the whole dish fails.


    Use mozzarella
    from buffalo milk, as fresh as you can find. Slice, layer, a little salt and
    oil. Do not cook anything.


    When the ingredients are honest, the cook only
    has to step aside.'
